  "observations": [
    "Opening the legacy no-pin project offline caused no write or permission prompt.",
    "The ordinary coordinate form saved only the selected project pin and one workspace revision.",
    "Back to project showed an empty FieldLog surface after saving and with a preseeded pin without writing. Package restart restored the dashboard and the same pin.",
    "The Android system prompt denied access and FieldLog reported the denial with identical workspace bytes.",
    "On a fresh install the user granted location through the system prompt. Android emulator GPS delivered the injected fix. The captured canvas showed coarse Natural Earth shoreline, a 50 km scale, a red saved pin, and a separate blue position marker.",
    "Location and backgrounding preserved workspace bytes and the position status cleared on return. A cold reopen retained the saved pin and Clear site pin advanced the revision once, preserving unrelated objects."
  ],
  "harnessCorrections": [
    "The coordinate editor exposes the range hint, with a separate nonclickable label.",
    "The system denial text uses a typographic apostrophe.",
    "The location shell help printed usage and exited 255. The granted case called its supported set-location-enabled route directly."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The standalone APK does not contain the later accessibility, save-recovery or dashboard dismissal corrections.",
    "The installed test used synthetic coordinates and an emulated GPS provider.",
    "TalkBack focus, approximate permission, large text, and interrupted save recovery remain open.",
    "The asserted standalone install is distinct from the Pair25 queue composition."
